## API

The app reads and changes the data with the REST API of the FastAPI app
that appgen generates from the same definition. `src/shared/api/` has
the client: `http.ts` sends the requests, and `http-store.ts` maps the
JSON names of the API to the keys of the TypeScript types. The build
variable `VITE_API_URL` sets the URL of the API (default
`http://localhost:8000`):

```sh
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 pnpm dev
```

The API must allow the origin of the app: set `CORS_ORIGINS` of the
FastAPI app, for example `["http://localhost:5173"]`. A table or a card
list sends its filters, its search, its sort, and its page to the list
endpoint, and loads one page. The related records that a view shows
(for example the owner of a project) and the boards load all pages.
{% if definition.auth %}
{% if definition.auth.password %}
The sign-in uses `POST /auth/sign-in` of the API, and each request sends
the token.{% if definition.auth.sign_up %} The sign-up page (`/sign-up`) uses `POST /auth/sign-up`.{% endif %}
{% else %}
Each request sends the token of the sign-in.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.providers %}
The button of a provider on the sign-in page starts the flow of the API
(`GET /auth/providers/<name>/start`). The API sends the browser back to
the page `/auth/callback` of this app with the token. The origin of the
app in `CORS_ORIGINS` also allows this page.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.password_reset %}
The pages `/forgot-password` and `/reset-password` use `POST
/auth/password-reset` and `POST /auth/password-reset/confirm`. Set
`PASSWORD_RESET_URL` of the FastAPI app to the page `/reset-password`
of this app, for example `http://localhost:5173/reset-password`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

