## Third-party APIs

{% if ts_apis %}
Each API of the definition without a secret has a client in
`src/shared/api/<api>/`: the TypeScript types of its schemas and a class
with one method for each operation that the app uses. An answer with an
error status throws `ApiError` of `@/shared/api/third-party`, and each
request stops after 10 seconds.
{% if react.api %}
The browser calls the API, so the API must allow the origin of the app
(CORS). A build variable sets the base URL of each API.
{% else %}
The app has mock data, so the clients send no requests: each call gives
the example answer of the OpenAPI document (`mock.ts`), after the latency
of the mock data.
{% endif %}

